  "id": "DrugBank_DB13874 - MONDO_grouped_18874_4643",
  "verbalization": "Enasidenib is implicated in the treatment of Myeloid Leukemia through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Enasidenib is associated with Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation, a subtype of Myeloid Leukemia, and that this condition is linked to Quizartinib and Azacitidine, both of which are indicated for Myeloid Leukemia. This indicates that Enasidenib may have a role in the treatment of Myeloid Leukemia through a chain of indications that ultimately point to the disease. The overlapping indications across these pathways suggest a potential mechanism where Enasidenib could be part of a broader therapeutic strategy for Myeloid Leukemia, possibly through targeting shared molecular pathways or biological processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering the broader clinical context in drug repurposing efforts.",
